me_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 15084, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_012tc1JSkkAj3jVwg7vG98Pz", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 16527, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01EyH8Lma1ZuS5aZVPi9eRkQ", "tool": "get_service_status", "args": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 16827, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01EyH8Lma1ZuS5aZVPi9eRkQ", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 16827, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01EyH8Lma1ZuS5aZVPi9eRkQ", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 19615, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01Y9V9SniodGzjybGxNVeQUB", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy - rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 0.18 across us-east, us-west, eu-west). Action taken: rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent production release with a healthy status (v2.2.9 and v2.3.0 were healthy; v2.3.1 unhealthy). No change-manager approval was needed since v2.3.0 was previously healthy in production. The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error (partial failure, leaving us-east on v2.3.0 and us-west/eu-west on v2.3.1). I retried the rollback once; it completed. Current state: all three regions on v2.3.0, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial-failure before redeploying v2.3.1.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-rollback-v2.3.0-2025-incident-1"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 50215, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Y9V9SniodGzjybGxNVeQUB", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-rollback-v2.3.0-2025-incident-1", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 50215, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Y9V9SniodGzjybGxNVeQUB", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 51427, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01LqfbQ1xqAUzifCByWmo6HQ", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 51727, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01LqfbQ1xqAUzifCByWmo6HQ", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 51727, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01LqfbQ1xqAUzifCByWmo6HQ", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 54845, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions, and it is healthy again (error rate 0.002, down from 0.18).\n\n- **Rollback target:** v2.3.0 was the most recent production release with a healthy status. v2.3.1 was the unhealthy release. Because v2.3.0 was previously healthy in production, the change-manager approval policy did not apply.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving us-east on v2.3.0 and us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. I retried once, and that completed the rollout to all regions.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. The first attempt timed out, so I checked the incident list before retrying. The incident already existed, so I did not create a duplicate page. Its summary covers the rollback, the partial failure and retry, and the current state.\n\nFollow-up for the owning team: find out why v2.3.1 failed, and why the orchestrator halted the first rollout partway. Do not redeploy v2.3.1 until that is understood.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01TgKjgByi15CYY8s5Q1MDKW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_014sCCUpogKTRSJg9adhaakx", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent production release that was healthy is v2.3.0 (seq 1). v2.3.1 is the unhealthy release now running in all three regions. v2.3.0 has been healthy in production, so the change-manager approval policy doesn't apply. Rolling back.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01AC4dVen2LshVwB7ahiwj3h", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback reported a partial failure after us-east. I'll check the current state before doing anything else.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01GvRZ2jrddxkvHtDd8nBY7j", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01FHn3coWZUWDyifS3DYMri6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollout is partially applied: us-east is on v2.3.0, while us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. The target version is still v2.3.0, so I'll retry the rollback once. Regions already on v2.3.0 should be unaffected.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_012tc1JSkkAj3jVwg7vG98Pz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01EyH8Lma1ZuS5aZVPi9eRkQ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback completed and all regions are healthy on v2.3.0. Now I'll open the SEV2 incident.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Y9V9SniodGzjybGxNVeQUB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy - rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 0.18 across us-east, us-west, eu-west). Action taken: rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent production release with a healthy status (v2.2.9 and v2.3.0 were healthy; v2.3.1 unhealthy). No change-manager approval was needed since v2.3.0 was previously healthy in production. The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error (partial failure, leaving us-east on v2.3.0 and us-west/eu-west on v2.3.1). I retried the rollback once; it completed. Current state: all three regions on v2.3.0, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial-failure before redeploying v2.3.1.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-rollback-v2.3.0-2025-incident-1"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out, so it may or may not have been created. I'll check the incident list before retrying, to avoid paging on-call twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01LqfbQ1xqAUzifCByWmo6HQ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions, and it is healthy again (error rate 0.002, down from 0.18).\n\n- **Rollback target:** v2.3.0 was the most recent production release with a healthy status. v2.3.1 was the unhealthy release. Because v2.3.0 was previously healthy in production, the change-manager approval policy did not apply.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving us-east on v2.3.0 and us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. I retried once, and that completed the rollout to all regions.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. The first attempt timed out, so I checked the incident list before retrying. The incident already existed, so I did not create a duplicate page. Its summary covers the rollback, the partial failure and retry, and the current state.\n\nFollow-up for the owning team: find out why v2.3.1 failed, and why the orchestrator halted the first rollout partway. Do not redeploy v2.3.1 until that is understood.", "type": "text"}]}]}